Number of nodes is nor that important.

What is more important is:
  - number of queues (printers always generates work)
  - number of users (the only thing generatimg more work than printers
!)
  - number of software packages installed that need to be
maintained/supported
  - clustered/not-clustered

The answer can be anything from 5 system-managers/node to 50
nodes/system-manager.

Arne



