Even if you were to get some sort of "Official" number, it would be
meaningless.  I know system managers that can manage hundreds of nodes by
themselves (with maybe one assistant so they can get some sleep) assuming
they have the time and money to set things up correctly.

I have also known system managers that would screw up one VAX so badly that
it would take two other system managers to go behind him and fix things.

So, your answer is somewhere between 1 admin per 100 VAXs and  3 admin per
VAX.

One thing I can tell you.  It will cost you less money and you would have a
better implementation if you were to hire one person for around
$125,000/year and an assistant for about $35-50,000 than it would be to hire
five system managers for $35,000 each.  Of course there are exceptions, and
you have to get someone who deserves the $125,000.

I could give you dozens of examples of  anecdotal evidence that would back
this up.  I have seen system managers make mistakes that kept production
clusters from booting for two days, and they got letters of commendation for
working so hard to fix the problem.   Read other letters on this board and
you will see that this is not uncommon.


