Managing a static VMS environment takes no time. Operator time is
required running backup and adding/deleting users.

Changing environments use manager time - planning, executing,
documenting and, occasionally, fixing. The only other work is dealing
with hardware faults.

User support however is an entirely different ballgame. If the users
expect the manager to know how to use, configure and bugfix all the
applications, compilers etc then you start to need multiple managers per
site, regadless of the number of machines. This factor is also a large
part of the reason why lots of support people are needed for PCs, not
usually for VMS. It's not so much the system as the user expectations.

-- 
Alan Adams



